#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124213 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/id #uuid "58966f53-5f83-5c86-8ffe-38ad0dffd2b3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12555" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1,$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =0,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124312 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/id #uuid "e85cfe0b-4ff6-5cce-9384-aeb930843b49" :question/math-academy-id "e-5265" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1,$ find the domain of $z = z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =4((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124364 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/id #uuid "1fbe37ed-9022-5c44-851c-0e66fe2fb79f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6078" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets \n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1\n$$\n\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4,$ we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+(z-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+1=-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bb29e98-356d-5e90-ac97-d29d6178c40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401455} {:answer/id #uuid "6a12cd1c-6682-5df8-923c-6c5944da1e21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401456} {:answer/id #uuid "6dea4a01-2c2d-5563-9522-56b73624cc0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-2)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401457} {:answer/id #uuid "9addb0b5-d438-50d6-917d-38fb314ead17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401458} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7a3e71-8adf-5c96-a5b6-a2346b9e5122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $z$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a12cd1c-6682-5df8-923c-6c5944da1e21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401456} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c38e30b-5bcd-54ca-8ea6-28e179828a4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b589cdc8-22e6-5881-b7f2-9fb3725db0fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-164272" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f1dbe88-840e-5aff-9deb-f75e1b1f7639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282233} {:answer/id #uuid "a22acf22-a5ab-5602-84be-6420e01a0cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,3-\\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(0,3+\\sqrt{2},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283106} {:answer/id #uuid "b48c092d-8b23-585e-bdfd-fd611ab6de43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,3-\\sqrt{2},0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283253} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f13bde-e930-509b-bef1-f3653a9c7dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283297} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7e3a0b-6169-5fdd-8aaf-8cd5f1e57223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,2,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f1dbe88-840e-5aff-9deb-f75e1b1f7639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282233} :answer-field/id #uuid "550c0a6b-52ae-54c2-84f9-fbc891ed0cb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf26d7e4-1a7e-56ee-a907-48a28ff7ba03" :question/math-academy-id "q-164277" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2}=-1,$ find its $y$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(0-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ 4+{y}^{2}-9 & =-1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-2$ and $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ccde34-ab5f-52ff-b240-f270b318cfc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281858} {:answer/id #uuid "1db9613a-b38d-5c22-a2d4-85361894a1e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281953} {:answer/id #uuid "497a54a2-6035-59d4-b836-921ac35b3c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4+\\sqrt{5},0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282312} {:answer/id #uuid "7d336f3f-44ae-5428-ae24-af0c092d2a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4,0,0)$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282771} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4338a0-f69f-5e33-b31b-69a65b201dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-4-\\sqrt{5},0,0)$ and $(-4+\\sqrt{5},0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db9613a-b38d-5c22-a2d4-85361894a1e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281953} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a25b654-47a9-5911-befd-5110ce7eae8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b3e714a-6331-583d-877a-3a1b6b241c29" :question/math-academy-id "q-164278" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $x$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5} & =-1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24f05d09-5866-526f-89e0-015abc3a350f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507643} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9e09ac-9afa-5c58-a5b6-e260d9ae3735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $z$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507735} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef7480b-38c1-599a-b433-084149902947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507786} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8befc7-a689-5d26-9fc6-529209bfcbe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507819} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf884f2-f6b1-51b5-8d26-4535c1ab921c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ef7480b-38c1-599a-b433-084149902947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507786} :answer-field/id #uuid "41b2046a-1076-5804-ad5b-bbdc2b3b7878" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10b62984-455d-5702-af01-c69ee89bcccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-164281" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{9} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-4$ and $z=2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cf4b7cb-1775-583d-9652-c43d93862b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281808} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab0c32b-18e1-5b35-a03b-9b03adc7d788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507814} {:answer/id #uuid "c147bab5-dcbd-567a-bc0c-62bd9e31c5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507866} {:answer/id #uuid "c6eae583-dc2b-5ab2-972a-742524065419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507874} {:answer/id #uuid "fce30ea6-bd76-50a8-a2fc-a7c8a2ca924e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cf4b7cb-1775-583d-9652-c43d93862b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281808} :answer-field/id #uuid "30268e91-e0e3-5312-957c-639c02663c53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ebd90dc-fabd-5a9a-8a63-d3d14e481ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-164303" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =16(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "051774ba-959a-5c1e-a9f4-ba2f7128c841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281733} {:answer/id #uuid "3dcc081f-8c87-52c8-b3e1-e3a8a332e58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487686} {:answer/id #uuid "a77b95d1-fceb-5a52-bb2a-611c7c686bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487882} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c48da9-56f6-56f4-b48e-a9ee4cfebf84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487969} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f233b9-83c6-5d23-a7ab-9cd273335e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "051774ba-959a-5c1e-a9f4-ba2f7128c841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281733} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ed39c8-50b3-5c43-b5b6-cec23b5c61a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e42866d-b20f-5a25-a416-745497c6d775" :question/math-academy-id "q-164305" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-{z}^{2}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fcdf940-6360-5efc-815a-67685f2bcd39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487692} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2dd945-a79f-5959-bfa8-cdfafd1ac3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487834} {:answer/id #uuid "ad54fb20-d344-5be0-b621-c08138a7d222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487897} {:answer/id #uuid "c00ed966-6006-5b17-8212-cacd1e467d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487928} {:answer/id #uuid "c13ff75f-ea2e-5e78-b3fd-6dfe315f448e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fcdf940-6360-5efc-815a-67685f2bcd39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487692} :answer-field/id #uuid "751f8b2e-9f8a-59f7-8b55-6cf5ae31cd83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "756c31bd-d0b5-518e-8fa8-bf3e64b797d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-164306" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}-\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}-\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16} & =-1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1 & =\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(z+5)^{2}}{16} & =(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1 \\\\ (z+5)^{2} & =16((x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1) \\\\ z+5 & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1} \\\\ z & =-5\\pm 4\\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ba49e8a-88e3-5af8-a8ce-e622a094b2f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}-{x}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378936} {:answer/id #uuid "4a64ea4a-0ae8-515d-b05b-9ae803e04729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378937} {:answer/id #uuid "95afe498-6155-5b2e-a789-fae228068697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378938} {:answer/id #uuid "f44a2ba1-779f-59be-a3bc-5774fcb7c580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378939} {:answer/id #uuid "98cc0bb9-af80-5a84-b0db-28037e593ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a64ea4a-0ae8-515d-b05b-9ae803e04729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378937} :answer-field/id #uuid "e921bfde-26ef-54c0-a3aa-dc35ce0d78b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b4af7bd-0bee-5303-8db2-07166632d8d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-164376" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the hyperboloid of two sheets $-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{16} & =-1 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b48605a-6454-5aa7-a69a-ef377c0cbf05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282891} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0f0d82-b3ea-5911-b21a-816bf9b2987b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283059} {:answer/id #uuid "b08ecc0c-ad93-5f5f-b74f-cbee9a15869e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283217} {:answer/id #uuid "c402ab7a-92e1-5991-9d60-3a619c492c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-{x}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283397} {:answer/id #uuid "ea151d6f-102a-5731-a9fe-9ce808d99adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08ecc0c-ad93-5f5f-b74f-cbee9a15869e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283217} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f87243-dc4b-5f88-8c5d-4447e8e28f49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c89427b-fc60-5717-8e73-c405cf88965d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164377" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $yz$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac7f7db-7330-5f70-b44b-0a16642e187a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379748} {:answer/id #uuid "404962ea-ae53-523e-8578-4e18ffd72b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379749} {:answer/id #uuid "633922da-3095-5e82-9e5f-8fad74f47589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379750} {:answer/id #uuid "10fb918d-971d-54a8-8033-9f883cc2ecd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379751} {:answer/id #uuid "d8bb9646-fd66-553e-9be6-9ce8191f4ccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10fb918d-971d-54a8-8033-9f883cc2ecd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379751} :answer-field/id #uuid "825bf943-ab64-50a2-b92b-5d83e050d9e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8aee91d6-47ac-55b2-9a4b-9e60b88d1933" :question/math-academy-id "q-35409" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the hyperbola in $yz$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19db25b8-9147-5d40-92c3-e1ee457752e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $5\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402410} {:answer/id #uuid "92adda02-c08f-5b9e-9ca7-7b5e715dec45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $10\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402411} {:answer/id #uuid "e2db736f-4ea8-56f7-891b-c509424fd359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$36$ and $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402412} {:answer/id #uuid "9f15a555-a9e1-53df-8497-bf3f68b67562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402413} {:answer/id #uuid "735824d8-08d1-5577-8580-3661f12dcfc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ and $50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f15a555-a9e1-53df-8497-bf3f68b67562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402413} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5953799-7f13-59d3-bf0c-ab698c3e76ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de878af4-60e8-5b69-ad9a-b8c3044d2e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-35410" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50}=1$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8e8afc2-8552-5580-9508-def40136ceeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322848} {:answer/id #uuid "70f17460-a0d4-5287-abb4-a7a14abebf28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507763} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3f2b2f-aee1-5f7a-bf0b-2d4d8ee14ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507787} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff9fece-b264-5543-a13e-24bcc8f1b95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507802} {:answer/id #uuid "ea037c7d-5e1c-5139-8dac-7afde0a986e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70f17460-a0d4-5287-abb4-a7a14abebf28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507763} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a044707-d7b0-5dd0-8375-76402ffda1c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ed1ee8b-94bd-5dd5-9af9-ac794637faef" :question/math-academy-id "q-36465" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =9((x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf44a846-8458-5e2f-bef3-72cf87a6035f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intercepts of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3503321b-5862-586b-8df4-8f5359f56cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(3,0,0)$ and $(7,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507673} {:answer/id #uuid "58d2eb9c-609f-574a-a49a-f23703c4758e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-5\\sqrt{3},0,0)$ and $(5\\sqrt{3},0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507727} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e4424e-c714-595f-b617-bad4bcd7c52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0,0)$ and $(8,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507829} {:answer/id #uuid "c96da8f2-38eb-5b21-ac5f-641d8aad25c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-3,0,0)$ and $(3,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507876} {:answer/id #uuid "eb172f3f-f1b6-5859-a6a9-6d63d2826e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(5-\\sqrt{3},0,0)$ and $(5+\\sqrt{3},0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4e4424e-c714-595f-b617-bad4bcd7c52a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0,0)$ and $(8,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507829} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7a3d3c-5105-54a3-9154-3edb17af611a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a868cb2e-b1af-59f1-9123-572788886f02" :question/math-academy-id "q-36475" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{9}=1$, find its $x$-intercepts." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =5\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=2$ and $8.$\n\nTherefore,the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(2,0,0)$ and $(8,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124503 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b079a5ff-e73a-592f-b16c-8740682538f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Domain of a Hyperboloid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa1cdee6-ac73-548c-adcc-2f2217142d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340680} {:answer/id #uuid "278677bd-636d-5e6b-baa4-61d15bbe918b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507645} {:answer/id #uuid "27a941c5-178a-59ae-85cf-65febbfce639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507646} {:answer/id #uuid "7d19b694-4700-571e-bc5e-8170015e653a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507781} {:answer/id #uuid "b85f79a1-9c55-50f6-8994-c949dca618ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a941c5-178a-59ae-85cf-65febbfce639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507646} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd0265d-f2bf-5b7a-b5a0-01ae09a136be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c94f24ee-6291-5f63-846b-0a8b39098945" :question/math-academy-id "q-74015" :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1 & =\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1) \\\\ z-1 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{2}\\ge 1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124555 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d28eda1a-a90b-57e9-969a-eb36552e413e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Traces of Hyperboloids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24aee5fe-fd62-52f5-ab75-5fea862f4504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380010} {:answer/id #uuid "63871641-13a1-5cee-b48e-89391deb62a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380011} {:answer/id #uuid "fa006068-571c-54ef-9578-918fa3e659e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380012} {:answer/id #uuid "1699178b-9e32-57c3-bfa6-a1f9d4c5fad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{x}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380013} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb725aa-f748-549d-a5c4-7aaf02dfbf46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1699178b-9e32-57c3-bfa6-a1f9d4c5fad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{x}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380013} :answer-field/id #uuid "b04a1820-b8ed-503d-8991-aaef46e28edd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bf6e7d3-9652-5ec1-b1a6-6239642d7ff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74021" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-{x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the hyperbola in $xy$-plane."}]}
